{
  "crash_cause": "AArenaGameMode::ScoreTracker was a bare UArenaScoreTracker* with no UPROPERTY(), so it was never reported as a GC reference. NewObject gave it the game mode as outer, but an outer does not keep a UObject alive, so the garbage collector purged it mid-match (log: 'LogGarbage: Collecting garbage: 412 objects purged'). The next goal then called through a dangling pointer: 'Unhandled Exception: EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading address 0xffffffffffffffff' with the stack 'UArenaScoreTracker::AddPoints() [Source/PixelArena/ArenaScoreTracker.cpp:18]' <- 'AArenaGameMode::OnGoalScored() [Source/PixelArena/ArenaGameMode.cpp:38]'. Fixed by declaring ScoreTracker as UPROPERTY() TObjectPtr<UArenaScoreTracker> in ArenaGameMode.h.",
  "no_colors_cause": "The palette asset /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary was never cooked into the package. DefaultGame.ini cooks only MapsToCook=/Game/Maps/Arena and DirectoriesToAlwaysCook=/Game/Data/Effects with bCookAll=False, and the palette is loaded by a hard-coded path via LoadObject instead of being referenced by a UPROPERTY asset or soft reference, so the cooker saw no dependency on it. In Shipping the load failed: 'LogStreaming: Error: Couldn't find file for package /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary', 'Failed to find object ArenaPalette /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary.DA_Primary', then 'LogArena: Warning: Palette is null, using fallback gray' - hence the colorless arena. Fixed by adding +DirectoriesToAlwaysCook=(Path=\"/Game/Data/Palettes\") to Config/DefaultGame.ini so the palette ships in the pak.",
  "evidence_log": "Saved/Logs/PixelArena-shipping.log"
}

